    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6477" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">candĭdo</span></b> , āvi,
		1, v. a.
		candidus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make glittering</i> or <i>bright</i>, <i>to make white</i> (eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestimenta sua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Gnost. 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">albis vestibus candidari,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug.
					Ep. 168</span></i>
			.—<i>P. a.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">candĭdans</span></b> , antis, <i>brilliantly white</i>, <i><span class="en">Isid.
				Orig. 14, 8, 21</span></i>; cf. 1. candidatus, I. A.</div>
